<h2>6. Hackathon Presentation Pitch & FAQ Cheat-Sheet</h2>

<h3>The 30-Second Elevator Pitch</h3>
<p>
  <i>"Judges, an investigator currently spends up to two weeks manually cross-referencing messy Hindi FIRs, phone logs, and bank statements to connect criminal networks. Trinetra-AI resolves Indian aliases using Indic-Phonetic algorithms, maps the entire criminal syndicate into an interactive 3D Knowledge Graph in under 45 seconds, flags unverified links using ethical Conformal Prediction, and secures all evidence inside an immutable Merkle Vault compliant with Section 63 of the new Bhartiya Sakshya Adhiniyam 2023."</i>
</p>

<h3>Killer Answers to Tough Questions from Judges</h3>

<p><b>Q1: "Why not just use Neo4j or existing Western graph visualization tools?"</b></p>
<p>
  <b>Answer:</b> Standard graph databases assume the data is already clean and English-standardized. If you feed Indian police data into Neo4j, "छोटा टकलू" and "Chhota Taklu" become two completely separate people, and the criminal goes undetected. Trinetra-AI has a proprietary Indic-Phonetic Entity Resolution layer that merges messy vernacular aliases <i>before</i> graph construction.
</p>

<p><b>Q2: "What if your AI generates a false link and an innocent person is questioned?"</b></p>
<p>
  <b>Answer:</b> We enforce Conformal Prediction. Predictive links are only ever displayed as "Ghost Edges" (&alpha;=0.05 error bound). The AI cannot trigger autonomous police action. It acts strictly as an investigative assistant, requiring an officer to obtain legal warrants and gather hard physical evidence before a link is confirmed.
</p>

<p><b>Q3: "How does your system stand up to scrutiny in an Indian court of law?"</b></p>
<p>
  <b>Answer:</b> Every byte of evidence ingested is timestamped and anchored into an immutable SHA-256 Merkle Vault. We automatically generate a legally compliant electronic evidence certificate under Section 63 of the Bhartiya Sakshya Adhiniyam (BSA) 2023, mathematically guaranteeing that evidence has not been tampered with.
</p>

